cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pulse-ep-decay, please cite the method paper (preferred citation) and this software."
title: "pulse-ep-decay: geodesic decay analysis of pace-mapping score maps"
abstract: >-
  Python package that measures how fast a pace-mapping score decays with
  geodesic distance from its maximum on a triangulated atrial surface mesh.
  Geodesic distances are computed with the Heat Method; a Gaussian fitted to
  the 2-mm binned radial profile gives the decay width sigma in millimetres,
  with a width class, an R2 flag for inadequate fits and a focality flag for
  disconnected high-score regions. A module for pulse-ep; the core works on
  plain NumPy arrays. The reproduction/ folder holds the scripts and archived
  result files behind the tables and figures of the method paper.
